> **Version note.** These three are the **pre-v10** builds (the `TravelRuleGate` constructor takes only `owner_commit` and `threshold_cents`; it is not linked to `PsavPassport`/`ComplianceRegistry`). The v10 contracts on `main` (cross-contract gate, two-key disclosure, signed sanctions lists) are deployed to preview first and will be redeployed to preprod/mainnet from there.

**How to interact**

- **CLI, preprod today (`scripts/agent.ts`)** — the preprod contracts above are driven by the ledger-v9 scripts as of commit `d434eab`. `scripts/agent.ts` seals compliance attestations on `ComplianceRegistry.attestCompliance` from a work queue (`agent-queue.example.json`):

  ```bash
  git checkout d434eab
  MIDNIGHT_NETWORK=preprod npx tsx scripts/agent.ts --once --queue agent-queue.json
  ```

  Env: `MIDNIGHT_SEED`, `BLOCKFROST_PROJECT_ID`, `PROOF_SERVER_URL`, `DPO2U_OWNER_SECRET` (see `scripts/lib/midnight-v9.ts`).
- **CLI, v10 gate (`scripts/travel-rule-v10.ts`)** — the operator CLI for the v10 Travel Rule gate: `attest-self`, `issue-passport`, `register-provider`, `evaluate`, `release`, `grant`, `approve`, `revoke`, `status`. It reads addresses from `deployment-<network>-v9.json` and requires a v10 gate (`codeVersion` v10 in that file), so it applies to the v10 redeploy, not to the preprod gate above. Every command has `--plan`, which prints the contract, circuit, cross-contract calls and args without touching a wallet or the network:

  ```bash
  MIDNIGHT_NETWORK=preview npx tsx scripts/travel-rule-v10.ts status --transfer <id> --plan
  MIDNIGHT_NETWORK=preview npx tsx scripts/travel-rule-v10.ts evaluate --transfer <id> \
      --policy <hex|label> --witness-file <file> --sanctions-list <file|->
  ```

- **WebUI (`deploy-console/`)** — a Vite browser console that deploys the contracts through the Midnight Lace wallet (Lace syncs inside the extension, so no headless full sync). Setup in [`deploy-console/RUNBOOK.md`](deploy-console/RUNBOOK.md): `cd deploy-console && npm install && npm run dev` → http://127.0.0.1:5173, with a local proof server on `:6300`.

### Follow-ups (out of scope for this consolidation)
